      "location": "Statement",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The Statement asserts: “For B≠∅, it is not an unrestricted Poisson law.” Take d=1 and the even Borel potential φ(0)=+∞, φ(x)=1 for 0<|x|≤1, and φ(x)=0 for |x|>1. It satisfies the in-scope definition’s superstability condition with φ_s=0, φ_r=φ, r_0=1, δ=1, and is regular with zero far-tail envelope. Its singularity set is B={0}. The definition restricts configurations to simple point sets, so every pair displacement is nonzero and the retained-admissibility indicator is identically one. The β=0 weight is therefore z^N, whose normalized law is the unrestricted activity-z Poisson law. This contradicts the stated implication for every nonempty B.",
